diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..1b60c83 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -2,6 +2,16 @@
 
 Webhooks notify another application when something happens on a board. Only account admins can list, view, create, update, delete, or reactivate webhooks.
 
+## Receiving events
+
+For each subscribed event, Fizzy queues one delivery per active webhook on that board. The receiver gets an HTTP POST with the event's `id`, `action`, `created_at`, `board`, `creator`, and `eventable` (card or comment) as JSON. Recognized Slack and Campfire endpoints get chat messages instead. The destination must resolve to a public IP address; redirects are not followed.
+
+`X-Webhook-Signature` is the hex-encoded HMAC-SHA256 of the exact request body, keyed with the webhook's signing secret. `X-Webhook-Timestamp` is the event's UTC creation time. The event ID is also sent as `Idempotency-Key`.
+
+Fizzy makes at most one POST attempt for a delivery, even if its background job runs twice. A timeout can mean the receiver processed the POST but its response was lost; Fizzy does not resend in that case. For exactly-once processing at the receiver, record the idempotency key alongside the change it triggers.
+
+A 2xx status is a success. Other HTTP statuses and transport errors count as failures. After at least ten consecutive failures spanning at least one hour from the first failure, the webhook is deactivated. A success or reactivation clears the streak. Delivery history is retained for one week.
+
 ## `GET /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/webhooks`
 
 Returns a paginated list of webhooks for a board.
